**Day 18: Backup & Recovery Basics**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to database backup and recovery using `mysqldump` for full backups, restoring from dump files, and simulating disaster recovery scenarios.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand the importance of regular database backups.  
• Learn how to perform a full backup of VolyoDB using `mysqldump`.  
• Practice restoring a database from a backup file after simulating data loss.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Perform a full backup of VolyoDB using `mysqldump`.  
• Simulate accidental table deletion and restore the database from the backup.  
• Document the backup and recovery process for future reference.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **Full Backup:** Captures the entire database state at a specific point in time.  
• **Disaster Recovery:** Restoring data from backups to minimize downtime and data loss.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `mysqldump -u [username] -p [database_name] > backup_file.sql`  
• `mysql -u [username] -p [database_name] < backup_file.sql`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Protecting against accidental data deletion or corruption.  
• Ensuring business continuity during server failures or cyberattacks.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• `mysqldump`  
• MySQL CLI  

**Summary:**  
Today’s session covered the fundamentals of database backup and recovery, emphasizing the critical role of backups in data integrity. Hands-on practice with `mysqldump` and restoration procedures provided practical experience in disaster recovery scenarios.  

